      "message": "@Luca here we go for `PS#3`:\n\n`stable-3.5:` before this change was able to handle `5` parallel calls (in `60s`  period of time) to:\n\n  changes/?q\u003dafter:%222018-01-01%2000:00:00.000000000%22+before:%222026-01-01%2000:00:00.000000000%22\u0026o\u003dall_revisions\u0026o\u003dall_files\u0026o\u003dmessages\u0026o\u003ddetailed_labels\u0026S\u003d20000\u0026n\u003d1\n\nand the initial `curl` to get the change in question took `15.748363s`\n\nafter applying the change it survived `7` which is `40%` better and initial `curl` took only `6.475330s` which is `~130%` better.\n\nI believe that this in combination with default `maxPages` and reasonable `maxLimit` (for anonymous group also being not able to issue a request with `no-limit`) would be the comprehensive answer to DoS threat, WDYT?\n\nI haven\u0027t tested it on `stable-3.4` yet as it requires a bit of conflict resolution but results will come.",
